Segmentation fault
```
I believe the issue is caused by invalid IL emitted by the Reflection.Emit member accessor. The converter implementation is incorrect, however we should detecting this error earlier and fail gracefully with a helpful error message.

review_comments:
Alternatively, we could decide to support this scenario by doing something like:
```csharp
                if (runtimePropertyType.IsValueType)
                {
                    Debug.Assert(declaredPropertyType.IsNullableOfT() || runtimePropertyType.IsNullableOfT());
                    generator.Emit(OpCodes.Box, declaredPropertyType);
                    generator.Emit(OpCodes.Unbox_Any, runtimePropertyType);
                }
                else
                {
                    generator.Emit(OpCodes.Box, declaredPropertyType);
                }
```
Which provides a quick and dirty fix at the expense of one allocation. Type errors would manifest as `InvalidCastException` which is consistent with how we deal with runtime type errors elsewehere.
